{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788809596628571001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bossy-skittish-foal","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"49c67ec3308f59cd9310a1d9c30f6ad7c9d9117a2eaedb09f162ea98298d2b1d","event_uuid":"f94afa0f-1561-44c2-904a-b20eada2304a","position":{"commit_sha":"ce4aa2de4fc6093935828190aa3abc20f3b15c7a","position":"1788804843321707098-f94afa0f-1561-44c2-904a-b20eada2304a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e4d5dc4df61820581ca0b56fc79b7c8be0c63e71803f23ca585283496290892f","event_uuid":"9e0d5667-a721-4947-86cd-234c295fc4b0","position":{"commit_sha":"e33b7ed3969fe0d442317a26e328c18a16a7aa74","position":"1788804919661516066-9e0d5667-a721-4947-86cd-234c295fc4b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788804843321707098,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9e0d5667-a721-4947-86cd-234c295fc4b0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"62dc-535b-5d05-421d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe cross-ticket overlap detector specified by ADR 0086 was switched off in this project on 2026-08-27 and 2026-08-31 (tickets eyeable-intimate-marmoset 62ab and horrendous-limpid-chamois 4eae) because its persistence and coordination design, a write-path enrichment queue that persisted digests and queue events on the shared `tickets` branch, produced write storms, lock contention, and unbounded store growth (105,197 of 147,074 event files are its sidecars). The operator ruled on 2026-09-06 that the retrieval pattern is right and the architecture underneath it is wrong: the implementation is removed, the store must keep parsing every historical event, the create-time same-title journal is re-enabled, and the redesign lives in a separate design-record epic. This is part of pre-1.0 breaking pass #4 and ships with release notes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No overlap or enrichment code path runs on any store write, plan review, or CLI invocation: the modules, the `enrich` verb, the 13 `[llm] overlap_*` keys and their env vars, the two prompts, the two schemas, and the doctor lock leg are gone. Checked by the grep and CLI assertions in the removal story.\n- [ ] A store holding all four retired event types (`TICKET_DIGEST`, `ENQUEUE_ENRICH`, `CLAIM_ENRICH`, `DONE_ENRICH`) still reduces, compacts, and passes `fsck`. Checked by the regression test the removal story adds.\n- [ ] The create-time same-title duplicate journal warns again on `rebar create` in this project, gated only by `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets`. Checked by two creates with the same title within the window.\n- [ ] Every doc, ADR note, and release-notes entry describes the shipped surface: ADR 0086 carries a retired status pointing at the design-record epic, the event-schema rows say \"retired producer\", and the release notes list every removed key, env var, and verb with its migration. Checked by the docs story's grep and heading assertions.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- Removal story: delivers criteria 1, 2, and 3 (code, config, tests, regenerated artifacts, the regression test).\n- Documentation story: delivers criterion 4 (docs sweep, ADR note, release notes, stale comments), depends on the removal story.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","62dc-535b-5d05-421d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"cea1-c784-99e0-446a","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Remove the overlap/enrichment implementation (ADR 0086), keep the store parseable, re-enable the create-time duplicate journal","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f94afa0f-1561-44c2-904a-b20eada2304a","9e0d5667-a721-4947-86cd-234c295fc4b0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788809596628571001,"uuid":"25250c1f-e5a2-4e1c-b376-80e4ca93695c"}